 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Of course. Make sure his room is the easiest one to find, and that his bed is the first thing you see when you enter. Keep routines as normal as possible. Use his favourite things where you can, like a favourite chair by the TV, or a photo album with his grandkids. If they things he enjoys, then yes. But keep it short and don't make a big deal out of it. That's understandable. Try not to take his behaviour personally, and don't worry too much about getting everything right. Just be kind and patient.",
